 "engineNeeds": [
  {
   "need": "lcd driver with a run-time mode, per-mode backplane slots, an output bank, and a data-pointer RAM load (action lcdload)",
   "status": "implemented and tested in the scratch copy: backend/src patch scratchpad/g2/pcf8576-lcd-mode.patch (converter.c/h, converter_int.h, converter_load.c, display_out.c/h, docs/parts-format.md; applies cleanly to main on 2026-11-23). Bench scratchpad/g2/pcf8576_family_test.c (187 checks incl. 14 loader cases) passes with it; the whole suite passes with it except the listing/trace goldens (additions only: 12 parts). Without the patch neither PCF8576 nor its devices load (`mode` must be a string, no `slots`/`load` keys, no lcdload action). Conflict note: plan-56-D's max695x-display.patch also edits display_out.c / display_out.h; applied after (or before) pcf8576-lcd-mode.patch it rejects 2 hunks of display_out.c (slots_of, apply, disp_timer lines) and 1 of display_out.h (context after bp_major). scratchpad/g2/pcf8576-lcd-mode-after-max695x.patch is this change rebased onto main + max695x-display.patch (apply that one first, then this one): built, the bench and every other test pass (only the listing/trace goldens differ, by the 12 new parts). icm7245-ascii16.patch applies after pcf8576-lcd-mode.patch cleanly.",
   "semantics": "display.mode may be {field, values: {fieldValue: static|1:2|1:3|1:4}}; display.slots: mode -> per slot the backplane pins driven (others Z); slot count = the mode's, frame time frameUs / slots; display.outputBank: field, nonzero + at most 2 slots -> slot k shows RAM row k+2; display.load: {pointer: field, step: {mode: columns}, bank: field (input bank), subaddress+hardware: fields (store only when equal, counter wraps modulo `subaddresses`), subaddresses: n}; protocol action lcdload: every following byte of the transfer is display data: bit j (MSB first) -> RAM column pointer + j / slots, row j % slots (+2 with the input bank in a mode of at most 2 slots), bits past the last column fall into the next device (counter+1) and are stored only if that is the hardware subaddress, pointer += step, wraps at the column count with counter+1. RAM stays 4 rows per column (ram stride = number of backplane pins).",
   "needed by": "PCF8576D, PCF85176, PCA85176, PCA85276 (and likely PCF8553 / PCA8553, BU91795, BU9796 in the same plan letter)"
  },
  {
   "need": "optional: write-only I2C slave",
   "semantics": "a bus/protocol key (e.g. protocol.writeOnly) that makes the address byte with R/W = 1 not acknowledged; the PCF8576D family 'will not respond to a read access' (pcf8576d p.27). Today the engine acknowledges a read address byte and shifts zeros.",
   "needed by": "PCF8576D family (host-visible only for a bus scan)"
  },
  {
   "need": "optional: per-byte NACK for display data not addressed to this subaddress",
   "semantics": "the chip acknowledges a data byte only while its subaddress counter equals its hardware subaddress (pcf8576d p.28, 'An acknowledgement after each byte is asserted only by the PCF8576Ds that are addressed via address lines A0, A1 and A2'); the engine acknowledges every byte.",
   "needed by": "cascaded PCF8576D family chips"
  },
