   "needed by": "PCA85176"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Three devices in lcddriver.json: PCF85176 (8 parts: PCF8576D x4, PCF85176 x3, PCA85176H x1; pinouts p56 TSSOP56 and p64 TQFP64), PCA85176 (the T parts, 110 Hz frame), PCA85276 (T1 pin, 2-bit subaddress, 200 Hz frame); 12 parts, all footprints existing (TSSOP-56, LQFP-64-10X10). The PCA85276 has no POR: the model starts in the PCF reset state (assumption). Frame times: Tfr = 24 / fclk typical internal clock; model frame = Tfr / 2 (6487, 4545, 2500 us). Part PCF8576DT/S400/2,1 is spelled as in the ordering table p.2 (probably a truncated ',118'); PCA85176H/Q900/1,5 as the sheet (and the task) spell it. obsolete flags: the ',118' / ',1' non-dry-pack reels (discontinuation notice 202107021DN) and PCA85176H/Q900/1,5 (DigiKey, per the task); PCF8576DT/2,518 is 'not for new designs' on the sheet but unflagged (it is the drop-in replacement). datasheets.json: 4 entries, URLs verified (PDF, byte-identical to the local files; need a browser User-Agent via python urllib, curl gets a 404 page). Bench pcf8576_family_test.c: pinouts, address table, power-on, 1:4 / 1:3 / 1:2 / static fills against the GENERIC-LCD glass (cells = RAM bits), Table 6 / Table 7 fills, C-bit command chains, banks, E bit, waveforms and pairing, frame times, subaddress counter, overflow, spill into the next device, PCA85276 2-bit counter, 14 loader checks; add logic_test(pcf8576_family_test) after display_out_test in backend/CMakeLists.txt. Goldens: parts / traces additions only (12 parts); no footprint change. The spec is planning/plan-56-data/specs/pcf8576-family.md."
